<title>CYPRUS: Strike delays flights at Cyprus airport.</title>
<headline>Strike delays flights at Cyprus airport.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1997-03-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Flights were delayed at Larnaca International Airport in Cyprus on Sunday night after a two-hour strike by workers, witnesses said.</p>
<p>The state-run Cyprus Broadcasting Corporation reported 140 workers went on strike at 7.00 p.m. (1700 GMT) demanding the reinstatement of two airport drivers suspended after an accident in the car park of the airport on Saturday.</p>
<p>The workers had also complained that they were not briefed by the authorities beforehand of an exercise carried out by Israeli security officials at the airport earlier in the day.</p>
<p>&quot;The strike was over by 8.55 p.m.,&quot; said Tasos Angeli, spokesman of Cyprus Airways, the island's national carrier. &quot;Some departures may be delayed slightly,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
